Build/
bin/
obj/
*.user
.vs/
.idea/
*.swp

# The gallery is generated, not written. Everything it is made of lives in data/ - the
# export, the pictures beside it and the metadata file beside it - and the web project
# rebuilds this folder from there before it builds itself. Committing the output as well
# would mean two copies of the same thing, one of which goes stale silently.
src/NmsVault.Web/wwwroot/gallery/items/
src/NmsVault.Web/wwwroot/gallery/index.json
src/NmsVault.Web/wwwroot/gallery/img/*
!src/NmsVault.Web/wwwroot/gallery/img/tech/
!src/NmsVault.Web/wwwroot/gallery/img/class/
!src/NmsVault.Web/wwwroot/gallery/img/favicon.webp
!src/NmsVault.Web/wwwroot/gallery/img/affinity/
!src/NmsVault.Web/wwwroot/gallery/img/move/

# tech.json, img/tech, img/class and the favicon are extraction output and ARE committed:
# extraction needs an NMSE checkout, the Pages runner has none, and re-running it against
# the same game version is byte-for-byte identical, so it adds nothing to history unless
# the game moves. The class badges are not optional decoration - they are how the site
# shows a class at all. The favicon is the S badge again, but squared off rather than
# trimmed to the shield, so it cannot simply be the published class badge.

.claude/
docs/
